From: Chufleco <80735658+chufleco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:09:52 +0000
Subject: phy: sunxi-cadence-combophy: enable CMN PLL1 clock on the DP+USB path

USB-C DisplayPort sinks that also use USB (Type-C pin assignment D,
STATE_D/STATE_F, i.e. either cable orientation: 2-lane DP + USB, e.g. USB-C to HDMI/DP adapters and USB-C
touch monitors) stay black on the Orange Pi Zero 3W. HPD, EDID and DPCD
are fine, but every boot logs:

  combophy0 dp wait pll enable timeout line:827
  combophy0 dp wait pll enable timeout line:845
  [EDP_ERR]: swing voltage reach max level, training1(clock recovery training) fail!

combo0_configure_usb_dp() never sets PHY_PMA_ISO_PLL_CTRL0
cmn_pll1_clk_en (0xe003 = 0x0003), so the DP PLL never locks. The
4-lane DP-only path (combo0_dp_set_rate()) performs this write for every
link rate, and the USB-only path sets PLL0 only (0x0001). Add the same
write to the DP+USB path, before the existing 0xe005/0xe006 writes.

One register write, DP+USB path only; DP-only and USB-only paths are
untouched. Tested on an Orange Pi Zero 3W (6.6.98-sun60iw2): the PLL
timeouts and the clock-recovery failure are gone, DP-1 trains at
5.4G / 2-lane, and a USB-C DP+touch monitor and a plain USB-C to HDMI
adapter both display (both were black before).

Upstream: https://github.com/orangepi-xunlong/linux-orangepi/pull/139
(issue #133), open since Sep 2026 with no response.
---
 bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c b/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
index 94c651e..9ebc5e6 100644
--- a/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
+++ b/bsp/drivers/phy/sunxi-cadence-combophy.c
@@ -2270,6 +2270,11 @@ static int combo0_configure_usb_dp(struct sunxi_cadence_combophy *combo0)
 		phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0x42EA << 1), 0x00F0);
 	}
 
+	/* Enable CMN PLL1 clock. The DP-only path (combo0_dp_set_rate) writes this
+	 * before the PLL-enable poll; it is missing on the 2-lane DP+USB (STATE_D/F)
+	 * path, so the DP main-link PLL never locks for USB-C DP-alt sinks that
+	 * also request USB (combo0_dp_phy_reset bit4/lane-ready time out). */
+	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xE003 << 1), 0x0003);
 	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xE005 << 1), 0x000B);
 	phy_writew(combo0->phy_reg + (0xE006 << 1), 0x2224);
 	if (combo0->orientation == TYPEC_ORIENTATION_REVERSE) {
-- 
